---
import MediaFrame from "./ProductMediaFrame.astro";
import AnimatedGif from "./AnimatedGif.astro";
import CaseMediaGallery from "./CaseMediaGallery.astro";
import sectionLibrary from "../assets/teebox/graphics/teebox-section-library.png";
import brandManagement from "../assets/teebox/graphics/teebox-brand-management.png";
import assetManagement from "../assets/teebox/graphics/teebox-asset-management.png";
import developerCodeView from "../assets/teebox/graphics/teebox-developer-code-view.png";
import translation from "../assets/teebox/graphics/teebox-translation.png";
import exportOptions from "../assets/teebox/graphics/teebox-export-options.png";
import previewResponsiveGif from "../assets/gifs/teebox/teebox-preview-responsive.gif?url";
import previewResponsiveStill from "../assets/gifs/teebox/teebox-preview-responsive-still.png";

const v1Limitations = [
  "Save emails or manage campaigns",
  "Automate quality checks",
  "Crop images or translate content",
  "Build dynamically with reusable sections",
  "Support multiple brands",
  "Maintain assets and campaign history",
];

const validationChecks = [
  "Images and links",
  "Missing content",
  "Spelling and grammar",
  "HTML validation",
  "Preflight warnings",
  "Export blocking for major errors",
  "Dark-mode simulation",
];
---

<div class="teebox-deep-content">
  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>A</span><div><p>Origin, research, and build vs. buy</p><h3>The product started with a repeated request, not a feature list.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="chapter-copy two-column-copy">
      <div>
        <h4>From service request to product opportunity</h4>
        <p>A small self-service gift-card HTML tool showed that repeated design requests could become reusable products. That led to a bigger question: if one recurring task could be simplified, could the same product thinking improve email production?</p>
        <blockquote>“I wish this could be easier.”</blockquote>
        <p>That became the working philosophy behind Teebox: understand where repeated effort was accumulating, then reduce it without removing the controls the team still needed.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Research before implementation</h4>
        <p>Before building, I reviewed the email-builder market to understand what existing tools did well, where they were limited, and how closely they fit the actual workflow.</p>
        <p>I compared customization, responsive behavior, accessibility, quality checks, brand consistency, reusable templates and components, email-platform requirements, ease of maintenance, localization, dark mode, and workflow fit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-panel">
      <p class="deep-label-small">Build vs. buy</p>
      <h4>Existing tools did not cover the full set of requirements.</h4>
      <p>Commercial builders did not provide the combination the team needed: flexible custom templates, responsive and accessible output, dark-mode support, built-in quality checks, localization, custom delivery logic, and code the team could maintain. The research showed what Teebox needed to handle and why an off-the-shelf solution was not enough.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>B</span><div><p>V1 and product evolution</p><h3>The first version solved editing. Each later version expanded the system boundary.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="chapter-copy">
      <p>V1 supported one Callaway template and exposed editable fields through a visual interface. It answered the immediate question, “Where do I edit this code?” However, it was not yet an email production platform.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="limitations">
      <div><p class="deep-label-small">V1 could not</p><h4>The first release deliberately left major workflow needs unresolved.</h4></div>
      <ul>{v1Limitations.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>C</span><div><p>Multi-brand system and management</p><h3>Shared infrastructure replaced independently maintained builders.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="chapter-copy two-column-copy">
      <div>
        <h4>One system, multiple brand expressions</h4>
        <p>Teebox uses shared components with brand variables instead of separate systems for each brand. Global variables, brand variables, templates, snippets, and reusable sections create one shared foundation that can grow without duplicating the entire builder.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Production work stays connected</h4>
        <p>The platform supports saved emails, lifecycle status, asset management, and campaign history. Supabase handles the backend for this management layer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <CaseMediaGallery label="Teebox system management views">
      <MediaFrame label="Reusable section library">
        <img src={sectionLibrary.src} width={sectionLibrary.width} height={sectionLibrary.height} alt="Teebox section library used to manage reusable email sections." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </MediaFrame>
      <MediaFrame label="Brand management">
        <img src={brandManagement.src} width={brandManagement.width} height={brandManagement.height} alt="Teebox brand management interface for maintaining brand-specific settings." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </MediaFrame>
      <MediaFrame label="Asset management">
        <img src={assetManagement.src} width={assetManagement.width} height={assetManagement.height} alt="Teebox asset management interface for maintaining reusable production assets." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </MediaFrame>
    </CaseMediaGallery>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>D</span><div><p>Quality, preview, and translation</p><h3>The system checks repeated issues, while people still own the final review.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="chapter-copy two-column-copy">
      <div>
        <h4>Preflight before export</h4>
        <p>Teebox checks repetitive production risks before delivery. Major errors can block export, but the system is designed to support human review, not replace it.</p>
        <blockquote>Automate repeated checks, not the final responsibility.</blockquote>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list" aria-label="Teebox validation capabilities">
        {validationChecks.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <CaseMediaGallery label="Teebox preview and translation views">
      <MediaFrame label="Responsive preview" motion>
        <AnimatedGif src={previewResponsiveGif} fallbackSrc={previewResponsiveStill.src} width={previewResponsiveStill.width} height={previewResponsiveStill.height} alt="Teebox interaction showing responsive email preview behavior." />
      </MediaFrame>
      <MediaFrame label="Contextual translation">
        <img src={translation.src} width={translation.width} height={translation.height} alt="Teebox translation interface for working with localized email content." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </MediaFrame>
    </CaseMediaGallery>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>E</span><div><p>Developer controls and delivery</p><h3>The visual workflow still preserves access to code and specialized output.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="chapter-copy two-column-copy">
      <div>
        <h4>Visual tools with developer control</h4>
        <p>Teebox moves routine production work into a visual system while retaining developer controls for the cases that require code-level work. The goal is to focus skilled developer time on transactional and automated email work rather than repeated manual production.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Delivery without separate builders</h4>
        <p>The same production system can provide plain HTML, Iterable output, and Responsys/RPL output for the previous email platform. Support for both email platforms was needed during the migration. Responsys/RPL support is expected to conclude in Q4. Shareable previews make review easier before final delivery.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <CaseMediaGallery label="Teebox developer and delivery views">
      <MediaFrame label="Developer code view">
        <img src={developerCodeView.src} width={developerCodeView.width} height={developerCodeView.height} alt="Teebox developer view showing code-level controls for an email." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </MediaFrame>
      <MediaFrame label="Export and delivery options">
        <img src={exportOptions.src} width={exportOptions.width} height={exportOptions.height} alt="Teebox export choices for Iterable, Responsys RPL, and plain HTML." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </MediaFrame>
    </CaseMediaGallery>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>F</span><div><p>Adoption and change management</p><h3>Building the product also meant introducing a new way of working.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="chapter-copy two-column-copy">
      <div>
        <h4>Rollout ownership</h4>
        <p>I owned communication with the teams involved, training, rollout, and the ongoing product direction. Testing was shared, and marketers and developers continued to provide feedback and requirements as the platform grew.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>How the team uses it today</h4>
        <p>The workflow has 100% adoption for marketing emails and supports approximately 14 emails each week across brands. Five separate workflow tools were consolidated into one internal platform. A direct report also contributed debugging and smaller post-launch features.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="adoption-strip">
      <div><strong>100%</strong><span>adoption for marketing emails</span></div>
      <div><strong>~14</strong><span>emails per week across brands</span></div>
      <div><strong>5 → 1</strong><span>workflow tools consolidated</span></div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="deep-chapter">
    <header><span>G</span><div><p>Architecture, learning, and roadmap</p><h3>The platform is designed to keep evolving without losing control of the workflow.</h3></div></header>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div><span>Backend</span><strong>Supabase</strong><p>Supports the platform’s saved work and management layer.</p></div>
      <div><span>System model</span><strong>Shared components + brand variables</strong><p>One shared foundation with brand-specific design.</p></div>
      <div><span>Delivery</span><strong>Iterable · Responsys/RPL · HTML</strong><p>One production system supported both email platforms during the migration. Responsys/RPL support is expected to conclude in Q4.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="technical-learning">
      <div><p class="deep-label-small">Early approach</p><p>Problem <i>→</i> prompt fix <i>→</i> implement</p></div>
      <div><p class="deep-label-small">Improved approach</p><p>Problem <i>→</i> understand dependencies <i>→</i> plan <i>→</i> confirm context <i>→</i> implement <i>→</i> test</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="roadmap-panel">
      <div><span>In progress</span><h4>Direct email-platform connections</h4></div>
      <p>API connections will link Teebox directly with email service providers to speed delivery and reduce manual handoffs. A future migration use case includes more than 100 automated campaigns that need rebuilding.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</div>

<style>
  .teebox-deep-content { margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .deep-chapter { padding-block: var(--space-4); }
  .deep-chapter + .deep-chapter { padding-top: var(--space-6); }
  .deep-chapter > header { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .deep-chapter > header > span { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 5vw, 4rem); font-weight: 500; line-height: 0.85; }
  .deep-chapter > header p { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .deep-chapter > header h3 { margin: 0; font-size: var(--step-2); }
  .chapter-copy { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .two-column-copy { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-7); }
  .chapter-copy h4 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .chapter-copy p { color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  blockquote { margin: var(--space-5) 0; padding-left: var(--space-4); border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-text); font-size: var(--step-1); font-weight: 680; }
  .deep-label-small { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }

  .decision-panel, .roadmap-panel { padding: var(--space-6); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); background: var(--color-canvas); }
  .decision-panel h4, .roadmap-panel h4 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .decision-panel p:last-child, .roadmap-panel p { margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); }

  .limitations { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(13rem, 0.38fr) minmax(0, 0.62fr); gap: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-7); padding: var(--space-5); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .limitations h4 { margin: 0; }
  .limitations ul, .check-list { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .limitations li, .check-list li { padding: var(--space-2) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .limitations li:last-child, .check-list li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .limitations li::before, .check-list li::before { margin-right: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-accent); content: "—"; }

  .check-list { align-self: start; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); }

  .adoption-strip, .architecture-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .adoption-strip > div, .architecture-grid > div { display: flex; min-height: 9rem; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--space-4); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .adoption-strip > div:last-child, .architecture-grid > div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .adoption-strip strong { margin-top: auto; color: var(--color-accent); font-size: var(--step-3); line-height: 1; }
  .adoption-strip span { margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-soft); font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .architecture-grid span { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .architecture-grid strong { margin-top: auto; padding-top: var(--space-5); font-size: var(--step-0); }
  .architecture-grid p { margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: var(--step--1); }

  .technical-learning { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-block: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .technical-learning > div { padding: var(--space-5); }
  .technical-learning > div + div { border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .technical-learning p:last-child { margin: 0; font-weight: 650; }
  .technical-learning i { color: var(--color-accent); font-style: normal; }
  .roadmap-panel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 0.35fr) minmax(0, 0.65fr); gap: var(--space-6); }
  .roadmap-panel span { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); border-radius: 999px; color: var(--color-text-soft); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.58rem; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; }

  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .two-column-copy, .limitations, .technical-learning, .roadmap-panel { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .adoption-strip, .architecture-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .adoption-strip > div, .architecture-grid > div { min-height: 7rem; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
    .adoption-strip > div:last-child, .architecture-grid > div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .technical-learning > div + div { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-left: 0; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .deep-chapter > header { grid-template-columns: 2.8rem minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .deep-chapter > header > span { font-size: 2.4rem; }
    .decision-panel, .roadmap-panel { padding: var(--space-4); }
  }
</style>
